# Vulnerabilities accepted after review. Each entry names the component, why it is not reachable,
# and when to look again. CI fails on any high or critical finding not listed here (SEC-18).

# picomatch 4.0.3 is a copy compiled into Next.js (next/dist/compiled/picomatch) and used for
# build-time file matching; no request-controlled pattern reaches it at runtime. Next.js 15.5.24
# is the latest 15.5 release. Re-check on every Next.js upgrade.
CVE-2026-33671

# Keycloak 26.7.5 bundles mssql-jdbc as 13.2.1.jre11, which is the fixed release for this advisory;
# Trivy reads the version as 13.2.1 and ranks it below "13.2.1.jre11". The driver is unused as well:
# the realm runs on PostgreSQL (ADR-0009). Re-check when the Keycloak pin moves.
CVE-2025-59250
